WEBVTT

00:04.087 --> 00:05.172
This is it.

00:05.255 --> 00:06.256
Please come in.

00:21.396 --> 00:22.356
Naotsugu.

00:22.439 --> 00:23.357
Mother.

00:24.274 --> 00:25.943
Is he a guest?

00:26.026 --> 00:28.820
Well, he...

00:31.490 --> 00:32.491
Pardon my rudeness.

00:32.574 --> 00:34.785
Please forgive my sudden visit.

00:35.285 --> 00:36.995
My name is Jinya.

00:40.541 --> 00:42.334
You're too polite.

00:43.085 --> 00:46.505
Naotsugu. May I ask who Lord Jinya is?

00:46.755 --> 00:48.173
Well, he's...

00:48.257 --> 00:49.925
I'm from Kadono.

00:50.008 --> 00:52.761
Do you mean the Kadono,
famed for their swordsmithing?

00:52.845 --> 00:53.679
Mother.

00:53.762 --> 00:56.431
Mr. Jinya is a kindred spirit
I've recently come to know.

00:56.515 --> 00:59.101
I invited him over for a drink tonight.

00:59.184 --> 01:00.769
I see.

01:00.853 --> 01:03.021
Well then, Mr. Jinya, let's go in.

01:03.480 --> 01:04.606
Please excuse me.

01:10.821 --> 01:11.989
Lord Jinya.

01:16.243 --> 01:18.203
You have my deepest gratitude.

01:18.287 --> 01:21.915
Have I done something
to merit your thanks?

01:22.457 --> 01:26.295
My son has been gloomy lately.

01:26.378 --> 01:28.630
But to see the light
on his face again today...

01:28.714 --> 01:32.217
as a mother,
there's nothing more reassuring.

01:45.522 --> 01:48.901
(Sword of the Demon Hunter)

03:08.981 --> 03:10.399
She's a good and virtuous mother.

03:10.482 --> 03:13.193
No, I'm sorry you had to see that.

03:18.073 --> 03:19.157
Here they are.

03:21.368 --> 03:23.537
So, they're daffodils.

03:23.871 --> 03:26.832
Is there anything special
about this type of flower?

03:26.915 --> 03:27.958
Not really.

03:28.041 --> 03:30.544
It's just that they're smaller
than I expected.

03:31.837 --> 03:33.088
Mr. Miura.

03:33.172 --> 03:36.341
You found these flowers in spring, right?

03:36.425 --> 03:37.968
Oh, yes.

03:38.051 --> 03:41.805
The girl that Sadanaga said he was going
to see before he disappeared...

03:41.889 --> 03:43.015
I think

03:43.098 --> 03:45.642
that girl might be a demon herself.

03:45.726 --> 03:46.643
What?

03:46.727 --> 03:48.020
Mr. Sadanaga

03:48.103 --> 03:51.356
was probably taken to a place
isolated from the real world.

03:51.440 --> 03:53.442
And these daffodils...

03:53.525 --> 03:57.321
Could these be the flowers
that grow where the demon lives?

03:58.280 --> 04:00.699
I'd like to see Mr. Sadanaga's room.

04:02.618 --> 04:03.452
Very well.

04:03.535 --> 04:05.037
Allow me to show you the way.

04:10.918 --> 04:12.336
What's the matter?

04:12.419 --> 04:15.255
Nothing. I'm sorry, but can you go ahead?

04:15.339 --> 04:16.215
What do you mean?

04:16.298 --> 04:18.550
In that case, wouldn't you lose your way?

04:18.884 --> 04:19.885
It's fine.

04:21.094 --> 04:22.262
I understand.

04:30.562 --> 04:32.523
Because if I'm there,

04:32.606 --> 04:35.108
maybe nothing unusual will show up at all.

04:41.907 --> 04:43.283
This scent is...

04:43.909 --> 04:45.160
daffodils?

04:46.745 --> 04:47.746
That's strange.

04:54.294 --> 04:59.466
One, look to the faraway shore.

05:05.722 --> 05:07.140
Father!

05:07.516 --> 05:09.560
Mother!

05:56.648 --> 05:58.275
Hey, look at that girl.

05:58.358 --> 05:59.484
Could it be...

05:59.568 --> 06:01.111
There's no doubt about it.

06:21.715 --> 06:22.758
I see.

06:23.967 --> 06:25.969
Papa is gone.

06:26.053 --> 06:27.596
Mama is dead.

06:28.305 --> 06:29.890
Our home is destroyed.

06:30.849 --> 06:32.434
Even our precious memories

06:32.518 --> 06:34.394
were ripped out at the roots.

06:35.437 --> 06:37.064
That's not all.

06:37.564 --> 06:39.066
I...

06:41.652 --> 06:45.572
I have even lost myself.

06:46.365 --> 06:50.410
I can't go back to that garden anymore.

06:51.078 --> 06:54.122
The path that leads there
no longer exists.

07:33.871 --> 07:35.289
I want to go back.

07:35.664 --> 07:42.087
I want to go back...

07:46.008 --> 07:47.926
I want to...

07:48.010 --> 07:49.595
I want to go back to that time.

08:00.397 --> 08:03.066
Oh, dear. You're having
so much fun, aren't you?

08:03.859 --> 08:05.944
I'm watching carefully.

08:06.653 --> 08:10.532
Father and Mother are here too.

08:17.414 --> 08:19.416
All things drift with time.

08:20.083 --> 08:22.085
Yearn for those bygone days.

08:36.850 --> 08:39.061
What... What is this?

08:39.144 --> 08:40.145
Mr. Miura.

08:41.396 --> 08:42.648
Mr. Jinya?

08:42.731 --> 08:46.944
It seems we've wandered into
a completely different place by mistake.

08:47.027 --> 08:48.737
Y-Yes.

08:48.820 --> 08:50.113
Where are we exactly?

08:50.614 --> 08:52.074
The sight of a spreading blaze,

08:52.157 --> 08:54.493
a girl who turned into a wandering demon,

08:55.035 --> 08:58.121
and the mansion she once lived in,
which should no longer exist.

08:58.747 --> 08:59.581
You saw them too, right?

08:59.665 --> 09:01.500
I saw them.

09:01.583 --> 09:04.920
So it seems those visions
weren't just daydreams after all?

09:08.757 --> 09:13.720
Two, homeland lost in the past.

09:17.266 --> 09:18.559
Brother.

09:28.151 --> 09:31.154
Well then, what should we have
for lunch today?

09:31.780 --> 09:34.700
Even I think my cooking skills
have improved.

09:34.783 --> 09:36.285
That's enough.

09:36.368 --> 09:38.245
It's time for you to go home.

09:38.412 --> 09:40.831
I'll make my specialty then,
some soba noodles.

09:40.914 --> 09:42.416
Listen to me carefully!

09:42.833 --> 09:44.918
You still have a family

09:45.002 --> 09:47.087
and a place to go back to, right?

09:47.546 --> 09:50.966
Don't let all this be ruined
over meaningless pity.

09:51.049 --> 09:52.593
Still, I've got to say...

09:52.676 --> 09:54.720
This is the Garden of Happiness.

09:54.803 --> 09:55.971
As long as I stay here,

09:56.054 --> 09:58.390
I can still see my father and mother.

09:59.099 --> 10:00.100
So,

10:00.893 --> 10:02.603
you don't have to stay here.

10:04.313 --> 10:06.356
You've got it all wrong.

10:07.482 --> 10:08.400
Listen.

10:08.483 --> 10:10.694
It's not the house that makes the people,

10:10.777 --> 10:12.905
but the people who make the house.

10:13.447 --> 10:14.281
So?

10:14.364 --> 10:17.159
If it doesn't make people smile,
it's not a home at all.

10:17.242 --> 10:18.327
What are you talking about?

10:18.410 --> 10:22.080
You've been here alone
for over 100 years, haven't you?

10:22.164 --> 10:25.167
You've known it in your heart all along,
haven't you?

10:25.250 --> 10:26.960
What you said...

10:27.544 --> 10:31.089
If you're willing to leave,
I'll leave with you.

10:31.173 --> 10:32.883
I can't do that.

10:32.966 --> 10:34.384
Besides this garden,

10:34.468 --> 10:36.929
I have nowhere else to go back to.

10:37.012 --> 10:39.264
Then do you want to live with me?

10:39.973 --> 10:40.891
Let's do that.

10:40.974 --> 10:41.808
Say,

10:41.892 --> 10:43.644
why don't you be my daughter?

10:43.727 --> 10:45.020
I'll quit being a samurai too.

10:45.103 --> 10:47.189
Let's go outside and live a carefree life.

10:48.273 --> 10:50.692
I can't escape from here.

10:50.776 --> 10:54.071
Besides,
I can't think of you as my father.

10:54.154 --> 10:56.448
Oh my, I've been rejected.

10:56.532 --> 10:57.741
But it's okay.

10:57.824 --> 11:00.661
I'm not in a hurry, so I'll slowly wait
until you change your mind.

11:04.456 --> 11:05.499
Just so you know,

11:05.582 --> 11:07.209
I'm serious about this.

11:07.292 --> 11:10.629
If someday you're willing
to think of me as your father,

11:10.712 --> 11:14.007
then promise me
we'll leave this place together.

11:15.050 --> 11:16.885
That day will never come!

11:19.263 --> 11:20.639
You leave me no choice.

11:20.722 --> 11:23.016
Then I'll stay here with you forever.

11:26.436 --> 11:27.479
What...?

11:28.105 --> 11:29.606
Where did my brother go?

11:31.608 --> 11:34.486
There's no one here anymore.

11:36.947 --> 11:39.867
There's nothing left
in this place anymore.

11:44.872 --> 11:47.708
Please give my brother back to me.

11:47.791 --> 11:49.209
I'm begging you.

11:54.131 --> 11:55.382
It's no use.

11:55.465 --> 11:57.050
Why do you say it's no use?

11:57.134 --> 11:58.218
You saw it too, didn't you?

11:58.302 --> 11:59.887
My brother was definitely here!

11:59.970 --> 12:02.014
He was here "before," wasn't he?

12:02.097 --> 12:04.308
What do you mean?

12:04.391 --> 12:06.768
Flowers bloom in their own seasons.

12:06.852 --> 12:07.853
What are you trying to say?

12:08.312 --> 12:10.480
Like what you showed me, Mr. Miura,

12:10.564 --> 12:12.608
the small daffodil
is an early-blooming variety.

12:12.691 --> 12:14.359
It blooms in winter

12:14.443 --> 12:17.487
but Mr. Sadanaga went missing in spring.

12:17.571 --> 12:19.740
And it's autumn now.

12:19.823 --> 12:21.491
Then where did Mr. Sadanaga

12:21.575 --> 12:24.620
pick those daffodils from?

12:25.078 --> 12:26.788
That's...

12:27.331 --> 12:30.834
In the demon's abode,
a place isolated from the real world,

12:30.918 --> 12:34.463
I thought the daffodils here
would always be in bloom.

12:34.546 --> 12:36.215
But that wasn't the case.

12:36.757 --> 12:39.343
Daphne odora is the flower
that announces spring.

12:39.426 --> 12:42.471
It's autumn now,
yet spring flowers are still in bloom.

12:43.180 --> 12:44.848
In other words, this place...

12:44.932 --> 12:48.018
Time passes faster here
than in the real world.

12:48.352 --> 12:50.521
Time passes faster?

12:51.522 --> 12:53.607
My power is called Dream Palace.

12:54.149 --> 12:57.194
It's an ability that can recreate
the garden of happiness I once lived in

12:57.277 --> 13:00.447
and project memories from that time
in this small world.

13:01.406 --> 13:02.324
But...

13:02.407 --> 13:03.367
Oh, dear.

13:03.450 --> 13:05.035
You're having so much fun, aren't you?

13:05.118 --> 13:06.870
I'm watching carefully.

13:06.954 --> 13:10.415
She's getting better at cuju.

13:11.750 --> 13:13.961
That's all my power can do.

13:14.044 --> 13:17.130
I can't trap anyone in this world forever.

13:17.464 --> 13:19.424
All I can do with this power

13:19.508 --> 13:21.593
is reflect on old memories.

13:22.636 --> 13:24.388
Then my brother…

13:24.471 --> 13:25.931
He's already...

13:26.181 --> 13:28.851
There's no one here anymore.

13:29.351 --> 13:31.395
How did this happen?

13:33.355 --> 13:34.857
This is goodbye.

13:34.940 --> 13:36.692
And I'm sorry.

13:37.359 --> 13:40.779
I took your brother away from you.

13:41.071 --> 13:43.323
But I still want to say thank you.

13:43.824 --> 13:45.993
It was Hyoma who saved me.

13:46.743 --> 13:49.621
Once you wake up,
you can go back to your world.

13:49.705 --> 13:51.331
So please be at ease.

13:51.915 --> 13:54.751
Little girl, what are you going to do now?

13:55.252 --> 13:59.506
I once fixated blindly
on all that had been lost,

14:00.215 --> 14:03.677
but he staked his life

14:03.760 --> 14:06.847
trying to become the home
I cherished most.

14:08.015 --> 14:10.475
That's why I...

14:14.313 --> 14:15.564
I see.

14:16.899 --> 14:20.986
You're going to carry out your promise
to Mr. Sadanaga, right?

14:37.044 --> 14:38.879
We're back.

14:40.088 --> 14:41.381
Why did my brother

14:41.465 --> 14:45.093
choose to stay in the world
created by that demon?

14:52.976 --> 14:56.897
The Garden of Happiness that's long gone?

15:02.486 --> 15:03.320
This morning,

15:03.403 --> 15:06.240
I went through the city archives.

15:07.032 --> 15:10.369
The Great Fire of Meireki
that occurred 200 years ago.

15:10.452 --> 15:15.457
It seems that the girl lost everything
because of that disaster.

15:16.583 --> 15:19.419
This is just my guess,

15:19.503 --> 15:22.506
but before the fire,
on the Miura family's land...

15:22.589 --> 15:25.717
It should be the mansion
where that girl once lived.

15:25.801 --> 15:27.594
You think so too?

15:27.678 --> 15:28.595
Maybe that's why

15:28.679 --> 15:33.767
the world she created is linked
to our mansion, don't you think?

15:35.185 --> 15:39.857
Calling this an encounter that transcends
time and space might sound beautiful.

15:42.776 --> 15:44.778
I'm sorry, Mr. Miura.

15:45.612 --> 15:49.074
In the end, I couldn't be of any help.

15:49.157 --> 15:50.951
Please raise your head.

15:51.034 --> 15:53.036
My heart is full of gratitude to you.

15:55.289 --> 15:56.290
My brother

15:56.373 --> 16:00.127
was, for better or worse, the type
to never waver once he made up his mind.

16:00.210 --> 16:03.922
I have no way of knowing
why he abandoned his family.

16:04.381 --> 16:05.883
But until the very end,

16:05.966 --> 16:07.843
he didn't betray his beliefs.

16:08.427 --> 16:10.137
That's all there is to it.

16:10.429 --> 16:12.931
Well then, it's almost time.

16:13.015 --> 16:15.726
I have to return to my post,
so please excuse me.

16:17.686 --> 16:19.730
Excuse me, Lord Miura.

16:19.938 --> 16:22.941
Your brother is truly an amazing person.

16:23.025 --> 16:24.026
What?

16:24.401 --> 16:26.695
Even if no one in this world remembers it,

16:26.778 --> 16:28.572
he still gave everything he had

16:28.655 --> 16:30.824
to save a child.

16:38.248 --> 16:39.291
Yes.

16:39.374 --> 16:41.210
I'm most proud of my brother.

16:48.842 --> 16:49.843
Jinya.

16:50.344 --> 16:52.513
Thank you so much for your help.

16:52.596 --> 16:55.015
Allow me to thank you as well.

16:56.767 --> 16:58.685
Your expression seems a bit heavy.

16:58.769 --> 17:00.270
There are still

17:00.354 --> 17:02.272
some unanswered questions
about this incident.

17:02.356 --> 17:03.357
Unanswered questions?

17:03.524 --> 17:07.528
That female demon called
Mr. Miura's brother Hyoma.

17:08.028 --> 17:12.407
But as far as I know,
his name should be Sadanaga Miura.

17:12.491 --> 17:13.909
The two names don't match.

17:14.076 --> 17:15.869
Say, sir.

17:15.953 --> 17:17.538
I think that's his real name.

17:17.621 --> 17:19.998
In other words, his imina.

17:20.499 --> 17:24.878
A samurai's imina is usually
only known by their lord, right?

17:27.047 --> 17:31.718
But if she's family,
it's not surprising that she knows.

17:31.802 --> 17:34.304
That girl called him Hyoma

17:34.388 --> 17:38.475
was probably because he
acknowledged her as family.

17:38.725 --> 17:41.395
Come to think of it,
you talked about this before.

17:41.478 --> 17:43.230
Mr. Miura's mother

17:43.313 --> 17:46.316
often scolded her son
who's obsessed with swords.

17:46.400 --> 17:47.234
What?

17:47.317 --> 17:48.485
I did say that.

17:48.569 --> 17:52.573
Would you mind telling me
how she scolded him again?

17:52.781 --> 17:54.908
Well...

17:55.409 --> 17:59.538
"Don't be so stubborn, Arimori." Even
his mother used to scold him like that.

17:59.872 --> 18:01.373
That was nothing.

18:01.456 --> 18:05.335
I just happened to hear it
from Lord Naotsugu's mother.

18:05.419 --> 18:06.795
I've met her before too.

18:06.879 --> 18:09.131
She's a prudent and dignified mother,

18:09.548 --> 18:12.301
and she was courteous
even to a ronin like me.

18:12.384 --> 18:15.095
She would never speak carelessly
in front of outsiders.

18:15.179 --> 18:18.015
And she always calls her son "Naotsugu."

18:19.474 --> 18:20.684
Well then,

18:20.767 --> 18:23.812
how did you come to know "Arimori,"

18:23.896 --> 18:28.066
a name that should only be known
to his lord or his family?

18:28.150 --> 18:30.611
About this...

18:30.944 --> 18:32.112
The female demon said that

18:32.196 --> 18:35.199
Mr. Sadanaga was no longer there.

18:35.282 --> 18:38.619
Demons don't lie,
but they tend to hide the truth.

18:38.952 --> 18:41.413
Therefore, this is my speculation...

18:42.664 --> 18:45.876
Mr. Sadanaga wandered into the world
created by that female demon by mistake

18:45.959 --> 18:48.921
and lived in that mansion
for over 20 years.

18:49.254 --> 18:51.882
But he decided to leave
in the middle of it.

18:52.633 --> 18:54.051
Then he realized

18:54.134 --> 18:57.387
that even though he had
been there for over 20 years,

18:57.471 --> 18:59.681
less than a month
had passed in the real world.

19:00.474 --> 19:03.018
Naturally, the Mr. Sadanaga
who had grown old alone

19:03.101 --> 19:05.354
could no longer return
to the Miura family.

19:05.896 --> 19:07.356
He went to the marketplace

19:07.439 --> 19:09.650
and bought an old house at a low price,

19:10.234 --> 19:12.819
then opened a soba restaurant
in the streets of Edo.

19:13.362 --> 19:16.281
Please correct me if I'm wrong.

19:16.615 --> 19:20.285
You said time passes quickly in the world
created by the female demon, right?

19:20.369 --> 19:24.164
If that's the case, wouldn't
Lord Sadanaga already be dead?

19:24.248 --> 19:25.374
That's impossible.

19:25.457 --> 19:27.793
How can you be so sure?

19:27.876 --> 19:30.170
Because the girl smiled.

19:32.256 --> 19:35.133
I don't think Mr. Sadanaga is dead.

19:35.217 --> 19:38.428
The reason she can smile is
because her father is still alive.

19:39.137 --> 19:40.264
Isn't that right,

19:40.347 --> 19:42.182
Mr. Sadanaga Miura?

19:43.976 --> 19:46.019
That's not fair.

19:46.103 --> 19:47.771
When did you find out?

19:47.855 --> 19:49.648
It was when all this came to an end.

19:49.731 --> 19:52.442
Though I had my suspicions from the start.

19:52.818 --> 19:54.319
Like his imina I just mentioned

19:54.403 --> 19:55.737
and this.

19:56.363 --> 19:59.867
A soba shop owner accepting a sword
accessory just doesn't feel right with me.

19:59.950 --> 20:01.869
This gift wasn't for the "shop owner"

20:01.952 --> 20:04.621
but for "Mr. Sadanaga," right?

20:04.705 --> 20:06.456
That's right.

20:06.540 --> 20:07.374
Arimori

20:07.457 --> 20:12.963
couldn't stand the way I always scratched
my head and thought it lacked decorum.

20:13.046 --> 20:14.923
So he gave this item to me.

20:15.382 --> 20:17.092
Won't you tell him who you are?

20:17.176 --> 20:19.344
He'll be happy to know that you're safe.

20:21.471 --> 20:23.515
Whether it's my family or that girl,

20:23.599 --> 20:26.768
in the end, I only kept
what I wanted to protect the most.

20:26.852 --> 20:30.105
From that moment on,
I lost the right to carry the Miura name

20:30.189 --> 20:33.192
or the right to call myself his brother.

20:33.567 --> 20:34.651
But...

20:34.735 --> 20:36.945
He's not a child anymore.

20:37.029 --> 20:38.155
Even without me,

20:38.238 --> 20:40.032
he'll be able to live just fine.

20:41.533 --> 20:43.911
Please accept the kogai, sir.

20:43.994 --> 20:46.413
It's useless to me now.

20:48.916 --> 20:50.334
You're so stubborn.

20:50.834 --> 20:52.169
I'm sorry.

20:52.711 --> 20:56.215
But he couldn't guess why I did it.

20:56.298 --> 20:58.383
Can you guess, sir?

20:58.467 --> 21:02.012
The reason I was determined
to be her father.

21:04.848 --> 21:07.559
You don't have a special reason, do you?

21:09.436 --> 21:10.604
Exactly so.

21:10.687 --> 21:12.481
It's not a big deal.

21:13.273 --> 21:18.028
I just couldn't bear to see her all alone.

21:18.111 --> 21:20.531
That's why I decided to stay with her.

21:20.614 --> 21:21.949
If you've made up your mind,

21:22.032 --> 21:23.408
you have to see it through

21:23.492 --> 21:26.119
even if others don't understand.
That's the way of a man, right?

21:26.912 --> 21:32.709
At the end of the day, no one can truly
understand the resolve you've made.

21:32.793 --> 21:35.128
That's true.

21:35.212 --> 21:36.713
There's no need for others

21:36.797 --> 21:39.633
to understand the beliefs in your heart.

21:39.716 --> 21:41.927
As expected of you, sir.
You're really perceptive.

21:42.010 --> 21:43.971
The accumulation of years
is truly remarkable,

21:44.054 --> 21:45.556
demon sir.

21:47.724 --> 21:50.853
I've been with a demon for over 20 years.

21:50.936 --> 21:54.022
I can tell just by looking at their aura.

22:01.780 --> 22:02.865
By the way,

22:02.948 --> 22:05.200
how is that girl doing now?

22:05.284 --> 22:06.243
What are you saying?

22:06.326 --> 22:08.662
She's right here.

22:13.166 --> 22:16.962
No wonder we were able to enter
the female demon's mansion so easily.

22:17.045 --> 22:18.881
Didn't I tell you?

22:18.964 --> 22:20.966
You're still a child.

22:21.258 --> 22:24.261
Compared to a demon
who's been around for almost 200 years,

22:24.344 --> 22:26.930
I'm still a child indeed.

22:27.014 --> 22:29.099
So, what are you going to do now?

22:29.183 --> 22:32.769
After all, your job is to slay demons.

22:38.734 --> 22:40.986
I'll have one kake soba for now.

22:41.778 --> 22:42.821
Sure.

22:42.905 --> 22:44.740
Father, one bowl of kake soba.

22:44.823 --> 22:45.824
Coming right up.

22:54.291 --> 22:55.918
Why are you laughing?

22:56.585 --> 23:00.005
I'm all smiles because my heart
is full of joy, of course.

23:00.088 --> 23:00.923
I knew it.

23:01.006 --> 23:04.176
The "I have nothing but that goal,"
from before was a lie.

23:05.469 --> 23:07.387
One kake soba, ready!

23:07.471 --> 23:08.805
Coming.

23:12.851 --> 23:16.563
Time washes all things away mercilessly.

23:17.064 --> 23:19.816
No one can hold on to what they love.

23:19.900 --> 23:21.610
It always slips through their fingers.

23:22.236 --> 23:23.695
What's lost

23:23.779 --> 23:25.197
is lost.

23:25.906 --> 23:28.325
It'll never return to your hands.

23:28.825 --> 23:29.826
But...

23:30.494 --> 23:32.120
Thank you for waiting.

23:32.204 --> 23:33.413
Here's your kake soba.

23:33.497 --> 23:35.624
I'm really proud of this one.
